                                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold font-heading mb-2 text-primary">Ellie's Law Advocacy Campaign</h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-600">
                                    Law

The UMKC Mission:Brain Chapter has joined forces with the Brain Aneurysm Foundation to support Ellie’s Law (H.R.902)—a bipartisan bill that would allocate $10 million annually to fund research on unruptured brain aneurysms through the NIH.

Named in memory of Ellie Helton, a 14-year-old who passed away from an undiagnosed aneurysm, the bill seeks to close the research gap and ensure studies reflect diverse patient populations.

Through advocacy, education, and events like our upcoming Gala, UMKC students are helping drive national support for this life-saving legislation—because awareness alone isn’t enough; research saves lives.


                                </p>
